  <data name="HierarchyCleanupConfirmTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Collapse hierarchy tags in watched photos?</value></data>
  <data name="HierarchyCleanupConfirmMessage" xml:space="preserve"><value>This scans indexed photos in all watched folders, including legacy automatic tags stored only in the cache, and saves the cleaned tags with each photo. Existing portable tag provenance stays authoritative; stale cache rows are reconciled to it. For example, Auto, Auto/animal, and Auto/animal/dog become only Auto/animal/dog. Sibling branches and unrelated tags are kept. A prefix is removed even if you originally entered it independently. Photo, existing XMP, and original cached-tag backups are retained before each change. Unavailable or unreadable files are skipped and reported. This cannot be undone from the tag panel; use the backups to recover removed keywords.</value></data>
  <data name="HierarchyCleanupConfirmPrimary" xml:space="preserve"><value>Back up and collapse tags</value></data>
