  <data name="VideoTrimPolicy.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Exports a locally re-encoded H.264/AAC MP4; trim points are rounded to the nearest source video frame. Audio is re-encoded when present. Ratings, tags and descriptive metadata are copied to the new file. Subtitles, extra tracks, HDR fidelity and camera-specific embedded metadata are not preserved. Windows must support the source codecs. Re-encoding removes keyframe-only trim limits. There is no fixed duration limit; processing time and output size depend on clip length and available storage. Existing files are never overwritten.</value></data>
